--[==[  MarkPresets  --  Saved Games\DCS\Config\MarkPresetsConfig.lua

  Edit this file, then restart DCS. Presets appear only while you are in an
  aircraft, never while spectating.

  If something does not work, set logLevel = "info" below and read
  Logs\MarkPresets.log. It prints the mission and server names as they load,
  says which profile matched, and explains anything it skipped.


  PROFILES  --  where a set of presets applies

    mission        = "Op Bandit"      that mission and no other
    missionPattern = "Bandit"         any mission with Bandit in its name
    server         = "Blue Flag"      that server and no other
    serverPattern  = "RotorHeads"     any server with RotorHeads in its name
    missionPattern = "*"              everywhere

  Give both a mission and a server and both must match. Give one and the other
  is unconstrained, so serverPattern on its own covers every mission there.

  The pattern forms match plain text anywhere in the name and ignore case, so
  punctuation needs no special treatment. Lua patterns work too, if you know
  them. Profiles are tried in order and the first match wins, so put specific
  ones above general ones.


  PRESETS

    name          the button's label. Left out, it is taken from `text`.
    text          what goes into the mark.
    {|}           where the cursor lands, so you can click the button and
                  start typing there. Never appears in the mark itself.
    {coords}      the mark's position, in the format the F10 map's
                  coordinate readout is showing. Click the readout to
                  change it.
    {elev}        the ground elevation at the mark, in the readout's unit.
    buttonColor   this button only.

  COORDINATES IN A FIXED FORMAT

    {coords_mgrs}      37 T FH 74461 49541
    {coords_dms}       42°52'53"N 41°06'23"E
    {coords_ddm}       N42°52.889 E41°06.394
    {coords_precise}   N42-52-53.37 E41-06-23.64
    {coords_metric}    X-00218471 Z+00562666
    {elev_feet}        91 ft
    {elev_meters}      28 m
    autoCommit    this button only.

  Coordinates are worked out from where the mark sits on screen, so they are
  as precise as the map's zoom: about half a screen pixel.

  A section can set buttonColor and autoCommit for all of its presets, and a
  profile for all of its sections. The nearest one wins.


  TEXT ON MORE THAN ONE LINE

  Either put \n where each break goes, inside ordinary quotes:

      text = "First line\nSecond line",

  or use double square brackets and press Enter where you want the breaks.
  Everything between them is taken exactly as written, so the later lines have
  to start at the left margin:

      text = [[First line
Second line]],

  A mark holds about five lines of 33 characters. Longer text has crashed DCS,
  so the log warns at startup about any preset that will not fit.
]==]

MarkPresets = {

  fontSize    = 11,         -- 6 to 32
  buttonColor = 0x1b1b1b,   -- 0xRRGGBB, no quotes, no alpha
  autoCommit  = false,      -- true: send on click. false: send when you click away
  compact     = false,      -- tighter padding and rows
  layout      = "rows",     -- "rows", or "strip" for one wheel-scrolled line
  logLevel    = "warn",     -- off, error, warn, info, debug

  profiles = {
    {
      missionPattern = "*",
      -- serverPattern = "RotorHeads",   -- and only on that server

      sections = {
        {
          header = "Contacts",
          presets = {
            { name = "SAM",      text = "SA-6 site" },
            { name = "Vehicles", text = "Vehicles: {|}" },
            { text = "Troops in the open" },
            { name = "Position", text = "{coords}\nElev {elev}\n{|}" },
          },
        },

        {
          header = "Status",
          buttonColor = 0x203040,
          presets = {
            { name = "Clear",   text = "Area clear" },
            { name = "SPOTTED", text = "SPOTTED", autoCommit = true },
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
